# Paths are ANCHORED with a leading slash. This is load-bearing, not style.
#
# This file used to read `supabase/`, unanchored, which matches a directory of
# that name AT ANY DEPTH. The intended target was the root `supabase/` folder
# of migrations and edge functions. What it also matched was `src/lib/supabase/`,
# the thirteen modules that build every Supabase client in the app.
#
# The result was a build that passed locally and failed on Vercel, every time,
# with `module-not-found` in what looked like "all server actions": 155 files
# import `@/lib/supabase/*`, and the directory was being deleted from the upload
# before the build ever started. The log said so in one line that scrolls past
# above the errors: `Removed 392 ignored files defined in .vercelignore`.
#
# `e2e/` had the same shape. It has no nested twin today, but anchoring it costs
# nothing and stops the next `src/**/e2e/` from silently disappearing.
#
# Rule for anything added here: if it names a directory that could plausibly
# exist under src/, anchor it.
#
# 04.10.2026: this file was replaced wholesale by an unanchored list that read
# `refs`, `docs`, `claude`, dropped the `.env.local` rule, and so dropped
# `refs/electro-checkout-text.json`, which `src/lib/checkout/electro-content.ts`
# imports. Five production builds in a row died on that one `Module not found`
# while `pnpm build` passed locally. The anchored file is restored below and the
# upload-size trims are re-added anchored, with the one ledger re-included.
# `refs/*` (contents, not the directory) is what makes the `!` re-include legal
# under gitignore semantics; `/refs/` as a directory rule could not be undone.

/.env.local
/.env*.local
# Local backups and the production override file carry local values; the
# deployment reads its variables from the Vercel project, never from an upload.
/.env.local.*
/.env.production

# Root-level only. NOT src/lib/supabase/, which the app imports 155 times.
# NOT `/supabase/` as a whole any more. `src/lib/payments/settlement-known-issues.ts`
# IMPORTS `supabase/settlement-known-issues.json`, and gitignore semantics
# cannot re-include a file under an excluded directory, so the whole-directory
# rule made every Vercel build fail with `Module not found` while `pnpm build`
# passed locally (measured 22.09.2026: the three latest previews of the
# `kenyonexpress` project, all Error, all that one line). The subdirectories
# are named instead; the JSON ledgers at the root of supabase/ ship.
/supabase/.temp/
/supabase/functions/
/supabase/migrations/
/supabase/schedules/
/supabase/seed/
/supabase/seed-fixes/
/e2e/
/.husky/

# Upload-size trims (04.10.2026). Nothing shipped imports these, except the one
# checkout ledger under refs/, which is re-included on the next line.
/refs/*
!/refs/electro-checkout-text.json
/docs/
/claude/
/migrations/applied/
/coverage/
/test-results/
/playwright-report/
/.vscode/
/.cursor/
/.turbo/
/.pnpm-store/
*.log

# Test and config files, safe to strip: nothing shipped imports them.
**/*.test.ts
**/*.test.tsx
**/*.spec.ts
**/*.spec.tsx
/vitest.config.ts
/playwright.config.ts
/biome.json
